@startuml
title Tickframe Deployment View - Docker Compose Runtime
skinparam shadowing false

legend right
  Deployment-view notation
  Node = machine, network boundary, or runtime container
  Database cylinder = stateful datastore
  Folder = persistent volume or configuration boundary
  Cloud = external public service
  Solid arrow = runtime network path
  Dashed arrow = configuration or mounted persistence relation
endlegend

actor "app user" as Browser
cloud "Binance and Bybit APIs" as Exchanges

node "VM" as Host {
  node "Optional host reverse proxy\nHTTPS/WSS termination" as Proxy

  node "Docker Compose project network" as Compose {
    node "frontend container\nNginx + built React app\nport 4173 -> 80" as Frontend
    node "backend container\nBusiness Logic App:\nFastAPI + collectors\nport 8000" as Backend
    database "timescaledb container\nPostgreSQL + TimescaleDB\nprivate port 5432" as Timescale
    node "prometheus container\nport 9090" as Prometheus
    node "grafana container\nport 3000" as Grafana
  }

  folder ".env private runtime\nconfiguration" as Env
  folder ".env.example committed\nsanitized template" as EnvExample
  folder "tickframe-timescale-data" as TimescaleVolume
  folder "tickframe-prometheus-data" as PromVolume
  folder "tickframe-grafana-data" as GrafVolume
}

Browser --> Proxy : HTTPS / WSS
Proxy --> Frontend : serves product UI
Browser --> Frontend : local HTTP when no proxy
Frontend --> Backend : REST JSON and WebSocket proxy
Backend --> Exchanges : public REST and WebSocket clients
Backend --> Timescale : SQL over Compose network
Prometheus --> Backend : scrape /metrics
Grafana --> Prometheus : Prometheus datasource

EnvExample ..> Env : documents required variables
Env ..> Backend : runtime URLs and thresholds
Env ..> Timescale : database password
Env ..> Grafana : admin defaults
Timescale ..> TimescaleVolume : persistent data
Prometheus ..> PromVolume : metric history
Grafana ..> GrafVolume : dashboards and settings
@enduml
